  "label": "Baboons are mapped as confused humans",
  "description": "The text 'you took us to the wrong mountain bro' implies human-like frustration and confusion. This is analogically mapped onto the visual of the baboons, who are depicted in various postures (sitting, standing, facing away) on a mountain ridge, suggesting a state of confusion or being misled. The meme uses the visual of primates to humorously represent human emotional states, creating a situational irony where animals are portrayed as if they are humans experiencing frustration.",
